# Generated marketing-video artifacts. Tracked vs ignored is decided by SIZE and
# REPRODUCIBILITY, not by whether the file is useful.
#
# docs/social-automation-plan.md is explicit about the reason: "every MP4 enters
# git history permanently. Deleting the file later does not shrink the history."
# At ~2-3 MB per 30s render across 1,136 tools that is several GB of permanent
# history, so rendered video and its intermediates stay out. Everything ignored
# here is regenerable from what is tracked, plus the live site.

# Rendered MP4s. The publisher uploads these to Zernio (7-day auto-delete) and
# they are never needed again.
renders/

# HyperFrames project folders — scaffold, staged media, captured PNG frame
# sequences and per-render output. By far the largest directory (63 MB for two
# tools) and fully rebuilt by make-video.mjs on every run.
hf/

# Screenshots + demo.webm per tool. Re-capturable at any time with capture.mjs,
# and deliberately re-captured rather than reused so footage matches the current UI.
capture/

# Generated voiceover / SFX / music working files.
audio-configs/

# TRACKED ON PURPOSE, listed here so nobody "tidies" them into the ignore list:
#   actions/        hand-written click scripts — real human work, not regenerable
#   briefs/         the publisher's input contract
#   creative/       per-video Gemini prompt + voiceover script; the editorial
#                   record of what each video actually claimed
#   master-plan.json, state.json   what has posted; the runner reads these to
#                   avoid reposting, and daily-post.yml commits them back
#   queue.json      the current one-item working queue
